          <compound>
            <id type="integer">79</id>
            <name>Fructose 6-phosphate</name>
            <hmdb-id>HMDB0000124</hmdb-id>
            <description>Fructose 6-phosphate is an important intermediate in the Carbohydrates pathway. The interconversion of glucose-6-phosphate and fructose-6-phosphate, the second step of the Embden-Meyerhof glycolytic pathway, is catalyzed by the enzyme phosphoglucose isomerase (PGI). In gluconeogenesis, fructose-6-phosphate is the immediate precursor of glucose-6-phosphate (wikipedia).</description>
